hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1887","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): Once I was extremely hungry, so I met Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and said, ""Recite to me such-and-such verse of the Qur'an."" He went into his house and recited and explained that verse to me. I left from there, and had not gone far when, due to hunger, I fell face down. I saw that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was standing by my head. He (peace be upon him) said, ""O Abu Huraira!"" I replied, ""Here I am, O Messenger of Allah! And at your service."" Then he (peace be upon him) took my hand, lifted me up, recognized my condition, and took me to his house. He (peace be upon him) ordered a bowl of milk to be brought for me. I drank from it, and he (peace be upon him) said, ""O Abu Huraira! Drink more."" I drank again. He said, ""Drink more."" I drank more until my stomach became swollen like a bowl. Then I met Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and told him about my hunger and my coming to him, and I said, ""O Umar! Allah chose a person to relieve my hunger who was more deserving of it than you. By Allah! The verse I asked you to recite, I know it better than you."" (Upon hearing this) Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""By Allah! If I had taken you to my house and fed you at that time, it would have made me happier than receiving red camels."
"1888","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Umar bin Abu Salamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that I was a child and under the care of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). At the time of eating, my hand would move around the dish, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""O boy! Say Bismillah, eat with your right hand, and eat from what is in front of you."" After that, this remained my way of eating always."
"1889","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, at that time we had begun to get dates and water to eat and drink to our fill."
"1890","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate thin bread and roasted goat until he (peace be upon him) met Allah, the Exalted."
"1891","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates in one narration that: ""I do not know that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ever ate in small bowls (cups, dishes, or plates), or ever ate thin bread, or ever ate at a (dining) table."
"1892","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The food of two persons is sufficient for three, and the food of three persons is sufficient for four."
"1893","(Nafi narrates that) Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) would not eat food until a needy person joined him in eating. One day I brought a needy person, he started eating with him and ate a lot of food. Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) said to his servant (Nafi), ""Now do not bring him to me, because I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'A believer eats in one intestine, and a disbeliever eats in seven intestines (i.e., eats to his fill).'”"
"1894","Narrated Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him): I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he said to a man who was sitting with him: ""I do not eat while reclining."
"1895","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never criticized any food. If he liked it, he would eat it, and if he did not like it, he would leave it."
"1896","Sahl (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked, ""Did you see refined flour during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He replied, ""Not at all."" (Then) he was asked, ""Did you sift the flour of barley?"" He said, ""No, but we used to blow off (the husk) with our mouths after grinding."
"1897","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that he passed by a people who had a roasted goat with them. They invited Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) to eat, but he refused to eat and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) departed from this world, but never did he eat his fill of barley bread."
"1898","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) once distributed dates among his companions, giving each person seven dates. He also gave me seven dates. Among them, one was spoiled (hard), but none of the dates was more beloved to me than that one, because it lasted longer while I was chewing it."
"1899","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the family of Muhammad (peace be upon him), since their arrival in Madinah, never ate their fill of wheat bread for three consecutive days until the Prophet (peace be upon him) passed away."
"1900","Narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): When one of her relatives passed away and women would gather, then after they returned to their homes, only the household members and close women would remain. She would have pots of talbina cooked, then tharid would be prepared and poured over the talbina. Then she would say, ""Eat it, for I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'Talbina comforts the heart of the sick and relieves sorrow.'"
"1901","Narrated Hudhaifa (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""Do not wear silk or brocade, and do not drink water from vessels of gold and silver (such as jugs, glasses, cups, bowls, etc.), and do not eat from plates (dishes, trays, etc.) of gold and silver, for these things are for the disbelievers in this world and for us in the Hereafter."
"1902","Abu Mas’ud Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that there was a man among the Ansar named Abu Shu’aib (may Allah be pleased with him), and he had a servant who was a butcher. He said to him, “Prepare food for me, for I will invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with five men.” Then he invited the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with five men, but another person also followed behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “You invited us five men, and this man has followed us. Now it is up to you; if you wish, you may allow him, or if you wish, you may not.” He said, “I have given him permission (i.e., let him also come).”"
"1903","Narrated Abdullah bin Ja'far bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him): I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) eating dates and cucumber together."
"1904","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): There was a Jew in Madinah who used to lend me money until my dates were harvested. Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) had a piece of land on the road to Bir Roomah. One year passed in which the land produced few dates, and that year passed. At the time of harvest, the Jew came to me, and I had not yet harvested anything from it (the fruit was very little). I began to ask him for a respite until the next year, but he refused. This news reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he said to his companions, ""Let us go and intercede with the Jew to grant Jabir a respite."" They all came to my orchard. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) began to speak to the Jew, but he said, ""O Abu al-Qasim! I will not give Jabir any respite."" When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw that the Jew would not agree, he stood up and walked around the orchard, then spoke to the Jew again, but he was still not satisfied. So I stood up and brought a small amount of fresh dates and placed them before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). He ate them and then said, ""O Jabir! Where is the hut of your orchard?"" I showed him the place. He said, ""Prepare a bed for me there."" I immediately spread a bed. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went there and slept. When he woke up, I brought another handful of dates. He ate them, then stood up and spoke to the Jew, but he still did not agree. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went and stood among the date trees a second time and said, ""O Jabir! Cut and give (the dates)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) sat at the place of cutting. I cut so many dates that the debt was paid off, and an equal amount was left over. I came and gave the good news to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), so he (happily) said, ""I bear witness that I am the true Messenger of Allah."
"1905","Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever eats seven Ajwa dates every morning, neither poison nor magic will harm him that day."
"1906","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When any of you eats, he should not wipe his hand until he has licked (his fingers) himself or has had them licked by someone else."
"1907","Narrated Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): In the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we did not have napkins (to clean our hands after eating). Our palms were all we had. (We would wipe them on) our arms, feet, etc. (We would rub them and then perform prayer, without performing ablution again.)"
"1908","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him): When the dining cloth of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was removed, he (peace be upon him) used to recite: ""All praise is for Allah alone, abundant praise, pure thanks, full of blessings. We could not fully fulfill the right of this food, nor has it been taken away from us forever (and this is done so that) we do not become heedless of it. O our Lord!"
"1909","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) finished eating, he would say: ""All praise is due to Allah who has given us food and drink to our fill. We could not fully fulfill the right of this food, nor do we deny this blessing."
"1910","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say that I know the reason for the revelation of the verse of veiling (hijab) more than anyone else. Even Sayyiduna Ubayy bin Ka'b (may Allah be pleased with him), who was a companion of high rank, used to ask me about it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had newly married Umm al-Mu'mineen Zaynab bint Jahsh (may Allah be pleased with her), and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) had married her in Madinah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) invited people to eat when the day had advanced. When everyone had left after eating, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and a few men remained sitting with him. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood up and left, and I went with him. When he reached the door of the room of Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), he thought that those people would have left, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) returned, and I also returned with him. (When we saw,) all of them were still sitting in their places. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went back again, and I went with him. When he reached the door of the room of Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), he thought that they would have left, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) returned, and I also returned with him. (This time) we saw that those people had (indeed) left. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed a curtain between me and himself, and (at that very moment) the command of veiling was revealed."
